# The agentic chat

`src/chat/` is the agentic chat — `<AgenticChat>` and everything under it — shipped from four subpaths of `@neofloai/atoms`. It came from the separate `@neofloai/agentic-chat` package in v4.3.0; the API is unchanged. It is a feature built *on* Atoms components, not a set of components, so the component rules (`30-components.mdc`) do not apply to it, and these do.

## Entry points and layers

| Subpath | File | Layer it may reach |
|---|---|---|
| `@neofloai/atoms/chat` | `src/chat/index.ts` | everything below, plus `ui/` |
| `@neofloai/atoms/chat/core` | `src/chat/core.ts` | `core/` only — no React |
| `@neofloai/atoms/chat/charts` | `src/chat/charts.ts` | `charts/`, `ui/kit/`, the headless layer, Recharts |
| `@neofloai/atoms/chat/mock` | `src/chat/mock.ts` | `mock/`, `core/` — no React |

| Folder | What it is | May import |
|---|---|---|
| `core/` | The engine: the chat standard's types, REST/SSE adapter, stores, persistence, runtime | nothing outside `core/` |
| `mock/` | In-memory backend on the standard | `core/` |
| `react/`, `registry/`, `blocks/` | The headless layer: provider, hooks, primitives, block registry, parsers | `core/`, React, `@radix-ui/react-slot` |
| `ui/` | The styled chat: shell, blocks, history, the kit | everything above, Atoms components, `react-markdown`, `remark-gfm` |
| `charts/` | Chart blocks | the above, `recharts` |
| `guide/` | The guide — Markdown, not code | — |

`eslint.config.mjs` enforces the table. Do not loosen a block to make an import pass; move the code to the layer that may make it.

## Imports inside the chat

- **Atoms components by their own module**: `import { Button } from '@/src/components/Button'`. Never `@/src`, `@/src/index` or `@neofloai/atoms` — a barrel import pulls every component into the chunk.
- **Icons from `@/src/icons/glyphs`**, never `@/src/icons`. A glyph the chat needs that is not listed there is one line added to `glyphs.ts`; see that file for why.
- **Tokens from `@/src/tokens`**, the theme type from `@/src/theme`, `useColorScheme` from `@/src/theme/useColorScheme`.
- **Never `@mui/*` or `@emotion/*`.** The chat builds on Atoms the way an app does. When Atoms lacks something the chat needs, the gap belongs to Atoms — add it there.

## Its dependencies are optional peers

`react-markdown`, `remark-gfm`, `@radix-ui/react-slot` and `recharts` are `peerDependencies` marked optional (and `devDependencies` for this repo). An app installs them only when it renders a chat. That promise holds only while nothing outside `src/chat/` imports them and while `/chat` never reaches Recharts — `npm run check:treeshake` fails the build otherwise. A new chat dependency is an optional peer too, `external` in `tsup.config.ts`, and named in the guide's install step and the changelog.

## The guide is the documentation

`src/chat/guide/<slug>.md`, one topic per file, listed in `guide/index.ts` with its title, summary, keywords and audience. `npm run generate` copies it into `data/chat.json`, which both the docs (`/chat/<slug>`) and the MCP `get_chat` tool read.

- **Write a topic once, in Markdown.** No JSX page per topic: `app/(docs)/chat/[topic]/page.tsx` renders every one. A topic that needs live UI gets it through `GALLERIES` there, not a page of its own.
- **No title in the file** — the page and the tool add it. Sections are `##`; their text becomes the anchor.
- **Link topics as `/chat/<slug>` or `/chat/<slug>#anchor`.** The docs render site links; `get_chat` rewrites them into the topic to request.
- **Code is pasted.** Every import must exist in the entry it names, from the four subpaths above or `@neofloai/atoms`, `/icons`, `/tokens`. Never `@mui/*`.
- Same reader-facing rules as every docs page (`50-docs.mdc`): no Figma provenance, no accessibility notes, no internal logs.
- A new topic: add the file, add its entry to `CHAT_TOPICS`, run `npm run generate`. The sidebar, the route, `get_chat` and `search_docs` pick it up.

## The MCP side

`get_chat` (`src/mcp/tools/get-chat.ts`) serves a topic per call and goes through the version gate. `CHAT_SINCE` is the first release with the chat: code is withheld from a project on anything older, because there every import fails, even where the shared gate would call the version "behind but fine". Backend topics are served whole — their blocks are wire formats, not Atoms code. `get_component` answers a chat export or a word in `CHAT_ALIASES` with a pointer to `get_chat`.

## What stayed outside

The backend conformance check (`runConformance`, the `agentic-chat-conformance` CLI) stays in the `agentic-chat-ui` repo as a standalone package, so a backend team checks its server without installing the design system. `guide/conformance.md` documents it; do not move it into `src/chat/`.

## Tests

`test/chat/`, run with `npm test` (Vitest, jsdom) and in CI. The engine is logic no docs page exercises, so a change to `core/`, `react/` or `mock/` comes with a test. `test/chat/setup.ts` stubs what jsdom lacks.

## Lint differences, and why

The chat's ESLint block turns off three React Compiler rules (`react-hooks/refs`, `immutability`, `set-state-in-effect`). The store hooks and the provider use the latest-value ref (`ref.current = prop` during render) on purpose, to keep `useSyncExternalStore` selectors and callbacks stable. Do not extend the exemption to other folders.
